[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2428857988","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98413#issuecomment-2428857988","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98413","id":2428857988,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QxW6E","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-22T10:07:09Z","updated_at":"2024-10-22T13:11:21Z","body":"TODO: Look at tests, add these cases to tests if they exist","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2428857988/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495117267","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98413#issuecomment-2495117267","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98413","id":2495117267,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UuHfT","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-22T23:59:45Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T23:59:45Z","body":"I don't think this is a good idea. Our goal is explicitly _not_ to carry over the entire GLSL preprocessing stack and take on that complexity. \r\n\r\nThe only pragma we support is `#pragma disable_preprocessor`, so we should error if anything else is used. In GLSL this doesn't provoke an error because vendor extensions can add pragmas and the code needs to be portable across vendors. That isn't the case for us, we fully control what pragmas a user can use, anything that we don't provide will never work. \r\n\r\nJust think about the simplest case here, let's suppose a user writes `#pragma disable_preprocesor`. It's an easy mistake to make, with this change, we would just silently ignore that error and the user will be left confused. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495117267/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495122603","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98413#issuecomment-2495122603","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98413","id":2495122603,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UuIyr","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T00:05:39Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T00:08:40Z","body":"@clayjohn The whole point of a `#pragma` is to allow forward-compatibility. It's like this not just in GLSL, but in C too (see linked issue). If the language wants to force new syntax to be recognized or else raise an error, then it should not use pragmas, instead create a new keyword or directive. Pragmas let you introduce behavior that doesn't break in previous versions. In fact, by this logic, `#disable_preprocessor` should have been introduced as a directive, not a pragma.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495122603/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495136576","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98413#issuecomment-2495136576","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98413","id":2495136576,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UuMNA","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T00:19:08Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T00:20:48Z","body":"An example of a `#pragma` that could be introduced later without breaking a previous version is an equivalent of GDScript's UID comment/annotation (if that gets merged) for shader files:\r\n```c\r\n#pragma uid \"uid://abcdef\"\r\n```\r\nIf this line has significance to the parser, it's better as a pragma instead of a \"special\" comment.\r\nSo it's like: process if you know what it is, else ignore.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495136576/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495545533","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98413#issuecomment-2495545533","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98413","id":2495545533,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UvwC9","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T17:15:34Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T17:17:37Z","body":"@clayjohn I agree with both points of view but in this case a question why pragma was chosen in first place? Just because it already was defined somewhere GLSL? Why not to use something different? I mean there is `shader_type <type>` which is not `pragma` and not preprocessor thing. It is a fully new thing of GD Shading Language. I mean you want to add something new. What will you consider adding something entirely new in terms of syntax like `shader_type` or somethng defined through `pragma`? It seems for me that you won't add anything to pragma anyway... Though as `pragma` is for preprocessor `disable_preprocessor` \"should\" be with `#`. So I agree with @geekley though not about concrete syntax of `#disable_preprocessor` but I agree with the idea in core","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495545533/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495643344","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98413#issuecomment-2495643344","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98413","id":2495643344,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UwH7Q","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T20:18:22Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T20:18:22Z","body":">  I agree with both points of view but in this case a question why pragma was chosen in first place? Just because it already was defined somewhere GLSL? Why not to use something different? \r\n\r\nI don't know why it was chosen, I'm assuming it was just to match the GLSL syntax. I also don't like it, but its too late to change it now. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495643344/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495872384","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98413#issuecomment-2495872384","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98413","id":2495872384,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Uw_2A","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T08:34:54Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T08:34:54Z","body":"Looks like won't be merged and I don't want to remember about it","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495872384/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551478489","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98413#issuecomment-2551478489","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98413","id":2551478489,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YFHjZ","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T14:34:56Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T14:47:30Z","body":"> by this logic, #disable_preprocessor should have been introduced as a directive, not a pragma.\r\n\r\n> I don't know why it was chosen, I'm assuming it was just to match the GLSL syntax. I also don't like it, but its too late to change it now.\r\n\r\n@clayjohn To be clear, I wasn't suggesting it should change now. Is perfectly fine to have mandatory pragmas. GLSL has it too. And the new Godot's flavor of GLSL (as per proposal https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11274, if accepted) will have mandatory pragmas too under a reserved prefix (and keep the others optional, as conformant to the standard).\r\n\r\nStill, the main purpose of a pragma is forward-compatibility in syntax, and it can only be done properly by allowing optional directives. When languages don't have those and need forward-compatibility, they have to resort to awful solutions like adding significance to comments or dangling strings like `\"use strict\"` in JS.\r\n\r\nSo, IMO it's better to implement it now rather than regret it later when for some unknown arbitrary reason the language needs some backwards-compatible feature. With this, at least it will be compatible from 4.4 onwards.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551478489/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551550473","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98413#issuecomment-2551550473","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98413","id":2551550473,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YFZIJ","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T15:00:26Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T15:09:11Z","body":"> let's suppose a user writes `#pragma disable_preprocesor`. It's an easy mistake to make, with this change, we would just silently ignore that error and the user will be left confused.\r\n\r\n@clayjohn This particular mistake is quite harmless IMO because if the user is doing it correctly (no other preprocessor directives), the behavior is the same with or without the pragma. If there is any other directive you may get unexpected behavior instead of an error, but it's extremely easy to see that you have a directive after that pragma on the same file (since not even `#include` is allowed). You can just CTRL+F `#`.\r\n\r\nAlso note that auto-completion already triggers for `disable_preprocessor` when typing.\r\nBut to be extra careful to avoid confusion, I recommend making the syntax-coloring mark recognized pragmas like  `disable_preprocessor` with a keyword color.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551550473/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]